Third-party tools ColimaUI drives but does NOT distribute
--------------------------------------------------------

ColimaUI detects and runs tools already installed on the user's machine. It
ships none of their binaries, so no redistribution obligation attaches to them.
They are named here because the app depends on their behaviour:

- Colima            — MIT License
- Docker CLI        — Apache License 2.0
- Lima / limactl    — Apache License 2.0
- kubectl           — Apache License 2.0
- Trivy             — Apache License 2.0 (image vulnerability scanning)

Security rule pack
------------------

The rule descriptions in `src-tauri/resources/rules/` are written by this
project. They reference identifiers published by external standards, and an
identifier is a fact rather than a work:

- CIS Docker Benchmark — © Center for Internet Security. Referenced by section
  number only. The free PDF is licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, which this project does
  not rely on: no CIS text is reproduced, adapted, or paraphrased here.
  "CIS Benchmarks" is a trademark of the Center for Internet Security. ColimaUI
  is not certified by, affiliated with, or endorsed by CIS.

- Docker Bench for Security — Apache License 2.0. Consulted for the numbering of
  the CIS sections referenced above. No code or text from it is included; should
  any be added later, its Apache-2.0 attribution belongs in this file.

The OWASP Docker Top 10 (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), the OWASP Container Security
Verification Standard (CC BY-SA 4.0) and NIST SP 800-190 informed the shape of
this work. Nothing currently shipped references or reproduces them; the idea of
graded verification levels is acknowledged, but ColimaUI's L1/L2/L3 definitions
are its own. If a future rule cites one of them, this file is where that is
recorded.
